# Every shell script here is executed inside a Linux container. A CRLF checkout
# makes the shell read `set -eu\r` and die with "set: illegal option -", so the
# stack cannot start at all.
#
# This is not hypothetical and not a preference: Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true in its system config, a fresh clone does not inherit the
# core.autocrlf=false someone may have set in another working copy, and without
# this file every clone on Windows produces unusable entrypoints — including
# docker-entrypoint.sh, which is what runs the migrations. Found by walking
# SETUP.md on a clean checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let text normalisation near binary payloads.
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
